    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Nestled within a choice, tranquil cul-de-sac setting just off Church Road, No. 15 Fuchsia Drive offers an exceptional opportunity to acquire a pristine home in the beautiful seaside resort of Ballybunion. Extending to a generous 110 sq.m - plus the magnificent bonus of a fully converted attic space ideal for a home office or games room - this end property delivers spacious and well-appointed accommodation throughout.\r\n\r\nThe ground and upper floors comprise a welcoming entrance hall, a comfortable sitting room, a bright kitchen/dining area, a practical utility room, a guest W/C, three well-proportioned bedrooms (including one en-suite) and a main family bathroom.  Every inch of this stunning dwelling is presented in turnkey condition, showcasing premium finishes and an abundance of natural light.\r\n\r\nExternally, the property is designed for relaxed living with a low-maintenance rear and side gravel yard, featuring a beautifully set down patio area positioned perfectly to capture the sun. Convenience is unmatched with private off-street parking, supplemented by additional adjacent set-down parking spaces. Enjoying a highly private yet accessible position, you are just a short stroll from Ballybunion’s world-famous beaches, leisure centre, vibrant local amenities and championship golf courses. \r\n\r\nViewing is highly advised to truly appreciate the sheer quality and layout of this coastal gem - contact us today on 068 21739 to arrange your private viewing."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Rooms",
        "SortOrder": 2,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall - 2.0m x 4.9m \r\nTiled floor and engineered maple flooring throughout the hallway, sitting room, kitchen/dining with red deal staircase and ample built-in underneath storage.\r\n\r\nSitting Room - 4.5m x 4.2m \r\nWith feature bay window, solid fuel open fireplace with rustic carved timber surround and cast iron insert - double doors opening into the kitchen dining area - also accessible from hallway.\r\n\r\nKitchen/Dining - 4.5m x 3.9m \r\nWith fully fitted maple kitchen, integrated dishwasher, electric oven, ceramic hob, extractor fan and tile splash back - overlooking the rear yard.\r\n\r\nUtility Room - 1.8m x 1.6m \r\nTiled floor, fully fitted storage with countertop, plumbed for washing machine and oil fired boiler - rear door access to your yard.\r\n\r\nGround Floor Toilet - 1.6m x 2.0m \r\nFully tiled floor to ceiling with toilet, wash basin and frosted window.\r\n\r\nFirst Floor Landing - 3.9m x 2.1m \r\nLaminate flooring and recessed hot-press with double door access.\r\n\r\nFamily Bathroom - 2.4m x 2.2m \r\nFully tiled floor to ceiling complete with bath with power shower overhead, wc, whb, mechanical wall mounted vent and frosted window.\r\n\r\nMaster Bedroom (Ensuite) - 5.3m x 4.0m \r\nSpacious ensuite master bedroom with laminate flooring and built-in recessed wardrobes. Ensuite - fully tiled floor to ceiling with electric shower, wc, whb, mechanical wall mounted vent and frosted window.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 - 3.9m x 3.4m \r\nLaminate flooring and recessed built-in wardrobe - overlooking the streetscape.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3 - 2.6m x 2.3m \r\nLaminate flooring and window over overlooking the streetscape.\r\n\r\nAttic Space/Landing Area - 1.3m x 2.1m \r\nWith access to storage space in the eaves.\r\n\r\nGames Room/Home Office - 5.0m x 4.2m \r\nWith access to eaves storage space and Velux roof light capturing views of the surrounding countryside.\r\n\r\nTimber Garden Shed - 3.0m x 2.0m \r\n\r\n\r\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Dwelling is in pristine turn key condition - fully alarmed.\r\n\r\nWithin a highly soft after choice cul-de-sac location just off Church Road within immediate proximity of all services and amenities including beaches swimming pool and Golf golf course.\r\n\r\nSpacious and light filled accommodation and 110 sq.m attic space - exceptionally well appointed and maintained.\r\n\r\nPrivate off-street parking and adjacent to additional visitor parking.\r\n\r\nBlock build house with double glazed PVC windows, oil fired central heating, solid fuel open fireplace and all main services connected.\r\n\r\nLow maintenance garden with gravel yard, sit down patio area with concrete post and panel finished with timber railing forming the boundary of the property - private and sunny aspect."
      },
      {
